                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First playthrough review time.\n\nI got A Bird Story as a gift from a Steam friend and played it without really knowing what to expect. The game is quite simple, and there is not much text or dialogue. Most of the story is shown through the scenes, colors, music, and small actions. I thought this was an interesting way to tell a story because you can understand what is happening without someone explaining everything.\n\nThe gameplay is very basic, so there is not much to learn or manage. You mostly move through the scenes and take part in small interactions as the story goes on. For me, the music and visuals were the main parts of the experience. The scenes are also quiet and simple, which gives the game its own style without adding too much to it. I didn't see any option to change the screen resolution or controls, so I played on the default settings.\n\nOverall, A Bird Story is a short game with a simple idea behind its storytelling. It does not focus on complicated gameplay and instead keeps things centered around the scenes, music, and visuals. I think its simple presentation is what makes the game stand out, even though there is not a lot of content to go through.",
